            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A method for configuration of a partition-resistant communication network is described. A request message is electronically transmitted to a plurality of computing devices. One or more agreement messages are received, each from one of the plurality of computing devices. One distant computing device and at least one local computing device of the plurality of computing devices are identified, such that the distant computing device has a greater message transmission distance to the processing server than the at least one local computing device. A communication connection is established to the distant computing device. Systems adapted to perform such a method are also described.</p>
            </abstract>
